  "id": "Compound::DB00678 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "Losartan is implicated in the pathogenesis of Persistent Dry Cough and Sinus Disorder through its interaction with Slc22a6, a transporter protein. The evidence suggests that Losartan, as an antihypertensive agent, may influence these conditions via the binding of its metabolites, Captopril and Enalapril, to Slc22a6. Both Captopril and Enalapril are organonitrogen heterocyclic compounds that bind to Slc22a6, indicating a shared mechanism of action. The presence of Slc22a6 as a target in both pathways underscores its role in mediating the effects of these drugs, potentially through the regulation of ion transport or other cellular processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Slc22a6 in the pharmacological response to Losartan, suggesting a broader role in the physiological effects of antihypertensive agents.",
